# TURN input inventory — no secret values

## Coolify / tenant values

```dotenv
TURN_IMAGE=coturn/coturn:4.17.2-r0
TURN_PUBLIC_IP=<public-ipv4>
TURN_REALM=turn.<tenant>.pmo.city
TURN_MIN_PORT=49160
TURN_MAX_PORT=49259
TURN_LISTENING_PORT=3478
TURN_TLS_PORT=443
TURN_LISTENING_IP=<public-ipv4>
TURN_RELAY_IP=<public-ipv4>
TURN_CERT_PATH=/etc/coturn/tls/fullchain.pem
TURN_KEY_PATH=/etc/coturn/tls/privkey.pem
TURN_TLS_SOURCE_DIR=<approved-coolify-or-host-managed-tls-directory>
TURN_AUTH_SECRET=<secret-reference-only>
```

`TURN_AUTH_SECRET` is a secret reference placeholder, not a value to commit or
paste into this file. The actual credential belongs in the approved Coolify
secret boundary/Vaultwarden workflow.

## Required records

- Coolify project UUID: `<record in tenant manifest>`
- Coolify server UUID: `<record in tenant manifest>`
- Coolify resource UUID: `<record after creation>`
- Image digest: `<record after pull/deploy>`
- TURN DNS A record: `turn.<tenant>.pmo.city → <TURN_PUBLIC_IP>`
- Provider firewall change: `<change ID>`
- Host firewall change: `<change ID>`
- Certificate reference and expiry: `<secret reference / date>`
- Credential issuer reference and TTL: `<component / duration>`
- Approved concurrent relayed viewers: `<number>`
- Transfer quota: `<provider plan / limit>`

Never put certificate bodies, private keys, HMAC secrets, credentials, cookies,
OTP codes or client media in this inventory.
